      "claim": "Tetrabenazine, a lower-similarity benzoquinolizine, has a mean oral bioavailability of only 4.9% in patients, indicating that related but structurally distinct molecules can have low F.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C33"],
      "claim": "Almorexant, sharing dimethoxyphenyl/amide and basic amine features but with lower similarity to the query, has an absolute oral bioavailability of 11.2% in healthy subjects, below 20%.",
